  "一把电吉他与一体式吉他音箱的实物照片。": "A photograph of an electric guitar and a combo guitar amplifier.",
  "Gain 与 Volume": "Gain & Volume",
  "Gain 主要影响前级增益和失真程度；Volume / Master 调整响度。不同音箱会相互影响，小幅转动、边听边调。": "Gain mainly affects preamp drive and distortion; Volume / Master adjusts loudness. Controls interact differently across amps, so make small changes and listen.",
  "普通音响与声卡": "Speakers & audio interfaces",
  "吉他接声卡的 INST / Hi-Z 乐器输入，再用电脑的音箱模拟处理，最后接声卡耳机口或监听音箱。普通线路输入与吉他输入并不相同。": "Connect the guitar to an interface’s INST / Hi-Z input, use amp simulation on the computer, and listen through the interface’s headphone or monitor outputs. A line input is not the same as a guitar input.",
  "耳机接哪里？": "Where do headphones go?",
  "接标有 PHONES / HEADPHONES 的耳机口。SPEAKER OUT 是给箱体喇叭的输出，不能接耳机或声卡。音箱与负载的具体要求按型号说明书来。": "Use the PHONES / HEADPHONES socket. SPEAKER OUT is for a speaker cabinet, not headphones or an audio interface. Follow your amp’s manual for speaker and load requirements.",
  "把声音接出来": "Connect your sound",
  "吉他、音箱、音响、耳机和声卡，分别做什么？": "Understand amps, speakers, headphones, and audio interfaces.",
  "让腿或背带托住琴身，琴颈略微抬起，肩膀放松。先让琴稳住，按弦的手就不用分心抓着它。以下以常见右手琴为例，左手琴左右对换。": "Let your leg or strap support the body, raise the neck slightly, and relax your shoulders. A stable guitar frees your fretting hand from holding it up. These examples use a right-handed guitar; reverse the hands for a left-handed guitar.",
  "单音先用指尖按弦，尽量靠近目标品丝、停在它的琴头一侧。手指弯曲，给旁边琴弦留出空间；拇指轻靠琴颈后方作支撑。": "For a single note, use your fingertip close to the target fret, on its headstock side. Curve the finger to leave neighboring strings clear, with the thumb resting lightly behind the neck.",
  "先轻按、拨一下，再只增加到声音清楚所需的力度。手腕保持舒适；感觉紧绷或不舒服就先停下放松。": "Start with light pressure, pluck once, and add only enough pressure for a clear note. Keep the wrist comfortable; pause and relax if it feels tense or uncomfortable.",
  "指法里的 1、2、3、4 是食指、中指、无名指、小指；不是品号。第 1 品在琴头旁边。": "Fingering numbers 1, 2, 3, and 4 mean index, middle, ring, and little finger—not fret numbers. Fret 1 is next to the headstock.",
  "放稳琴，轻轻按弦": "Hold the guitar; fret lightly",
  "用位置和放松换来清楚的声音。": "A good position and a relaxed hand help notes ring clearly.",
  "把食指自然弯曲，让拨片靠在食指侧面，再用拇指指腹盖住。露出一小截尖端即可，握到它不乱转，又能让手腕自由活动。": "Curl the index finger naturally, rest the pick against its side, and cover it with the thumb pad. Leave a small tip exposed: hold it steadily while keeping the wrist free to move.",
  "先选一根空弦，用很小的动作向下拨过它，再试向上拨回。让拨片轻轻越过琴弦，先听声音是否清楚，再慢慢扩大到扫弦。": "Choose one open string. Make a small downstroke, then try an upstroke. Let the pick pass lightly through the string; listen for a clear sound before widening the movement into a strum.",
  "拨片卡住时，减少插进琴弦的深度，稍微倾斜一点；拨片滑动时，只小幅增加拇指与食指的夹持力。": "If the pick catches, expose less of it to the string and try a slight angle. If it slips, increase thumb-and-index pressure just a little.",
  "去和弦图鉴看指法": "Explore chord fingerings",
  "先把琴调准": "Tune your guitar",
  "拿稳拨片，拨响一根弦": "Hold a pick; play a string",
  "小幅、放松，先听见一个干净的音。": "Small, relaxed movements. Listen for one clean note.",
  "沙沙响、打品": "Buzzing notes",
  "先把指尖移近品丝，再小幅增加压力；确认手指没有正压品丝。位置调整后仍持续打品，可能需要检查琴弦高度或琴的设定。": "Move the fingertip closer to the fret, then add a little pressure. Make sure you are not pressing on the fret wire. Persistent buzzing after adjusting your hand may need a setup or string-height check.",
  "旁边的弦不响": "Muted neighboring strings",
